From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 07:48:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: tps65217: do not require PMIC child OF node

The TPS65217 regulator binding models regulator constraints under the
parent PMIC node's "regulators" container. It does not define a
"ti,tps65217-pmic" child node.

The regulator platform driver still binds by the platform device name
"tps65217-pmic" and parses regulator constraints through the parent PMIC
device. Keeping an OF compatible on the MFD cell only makes mfd-core look
for a child node that the binding does not provide.

Drop the MFD cell OF match for the PMIC regulator child while preserving the
platform device name used by the regulator driver.

Upstream-Status: Pending [needs review against TPS65217 MFD binding]
Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/tps65217.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c b/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c
index 029ecc32f078..0f425f556834 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c
@@ -80,7 +80,6 @@ static struct irq_chip tps65217_irq_chip = {
 static struct mfd_cell tps65217s[] = {
 	{
 		.name = "tps65217-pmic",
-		.of_compatible = "ti,tps65217-pmic",
 	},
 	{
 		.name = "tps65217-bl",
-- 
2.34.1

